# Throwaway scratch, per bass/.bass/genesis.md's "Scratch files" section. The tracked .gitkeep
# makes the folder materialize in every clone and worktree, so nothing here can reach a commit and
# no cleanup step is ever needed before `git add -A`. Bare `tmp/` too -- a safety net, not the
# canonical name: `tmp/` is what an agent reaches for by instinct, and a `tmp_*/` rule does NOT
# match a bare `tmp`, which is exactly how a scratch file nearly got committed on 2026-09-05.
scratch/*
!scratch/.gitkeep
tmp/
